Fun fact: did you know Grayswandir doubles bonuses from rings of
increase damage? Let's just say I didn't... until now. My
archaeologist #twoweaponed the +6 Grayswandir and a +8 silver dagger
named Grayswandir Junior, together with +7 and +8 rings of increase
damage (sadly, the ring wasn't edible in my game).

The rest is nearly immaterial. I killed every living thing on Astral,
as well as a few unliving since I hadn't genocided arch-lichs yet.
Riders died from no more than three +7 darts at a distance, at basic
dart skill! I got cocky with Pestilence and almost died to his
sickness attack before I realized meleeing Pesty without stun
resistance was a bad, bad, fucking *bad* idea. But darts were
thankfully good enough.

The only thing better than Grayswandir and the rings was the orange
dragon scale mail. In Sporkhack, ODSM has a passive sleep attack that
ignores magic cancellation. Any monster that hits you is temporarily
slowed. I'd easily consider it the most powerful armor in the game.

"The Wizard of Yendor looks a little sleepy."
"Asmodeus looks a little sleepy."
"Death looks a little sleepy."

Get the idea now? Even Demogorgon wouldn't be a significant threat
slowed down, since my melee was powerful enough to kill the Riders in
a single round. Sadly, I didn't meet him. Next time...

Aside from that, did the protection run via credit cloning again -
helped that I found an aquamarine stone in a general store. Also,
*after* full 9 unit-(of protection) run, found bones file of...
myself, with two magic lamps, a bag of holding, and speed boots. That
was, er, game breaking. Rather than go for a speed run, I decided to
have fun making the Arc as buff as possible.

Well, I hope this short post has given you some evil ideas. ;)


